<Program Use="Context" Name="MainProgram">
<Routines Use="Context">
<Routine Use="Context" Name="MainRoutine">
<RLLContent Use="Context">
<Rung Use="Target" Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[============================================================
L_CPU_19:  LOGIX -- Processor Utilization (Major Rev. 19)
============================================================
Revision 3.1-01 Release  2014-09-03:  See V3.1-xx Release Notes for details.
V1.x and V2.x Revision History archived.
V3.0-00  2013-06-30:  Added Inf_Lib. Removed "Main Task" scan time information,
as this is now covered by L_TaskMon instances. Changed
Operator Commands (OCmds) to Maintenance Commands (MCmds).
V3.1-00  2014-06-30:  Unmodified for Logix Diagnostics Library V3.1, up-rev only.
V3.1-01  2014-09-03:  Unmodified, up-rev only for V3.1-01 public release.
============================================================
To gather diagnostics and metrics for troubleshooting performance issues,
enable the L_CPU instruction (OCmd_Enable)  Have the collected data
(in the Ref_Out tag, "L_CPU_Out") available when you call Technical Support.
When done, disable the instruction (OCmd_Disable) to minimize its
messaging impact on the running application.

***************************************************************
ATTENTION!!!    ATTENTION!!!
***************************************************************

BE SURE TO SET Cfg_SlotNumber TO YOUR
CONTROLLER'S CHASSIS LOCATION.

BE SURE TO ENTER THE NAME OF THE CONTINUOUS
TASK IN THE GSV "Instance Name",
OR DELETE THE GSV AMD SET
Cfg_ContTaskInstance to ZERO IF
THERE IS NO CONTINUOUS TASK.

BE SURE THESE ITEMS ARE COMPLETED BEFORE
SWITCHING THE CONTROLLER TO "RUN".

The L_CPU Instruction configures its MSG paths based on the configured slot number,
and it links to Task scan time data based on the "ContTaskInstance" returnd by the GSV.
If the MSG path is changed, the controller must be cycled RUN -> PROG -> RUN
for the change to be recognized!!!
.
The Update Time can be made faster or slower as needed.
Update Times of 2 seconds or faster are not recommended.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[MOV(0,L_CPU.Cfg_SlotNumber) GSV(Task,ContinuousTaskName,INSTANCE,L_CPU.Cfg_ContTaskInstance) ,L_CPU_19(L_CPU,L_CPU_Out,L_CPU_MsgSetWindow,L_CPU_MsgGetTrendObjUse,L_CPU_MsgGetMemUse,L_CPU_MsgGetOSTaskTimes,L_CPU_MsgGetUserTaskTimes,L_CPU_MsgGetConnUse,L_CPU_WindowTime,L_CPU_TrendObjData,L_CPU_MemUseData,L_CPU_TaskTimeData,L_CPU_PortCapyData) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
</Programs>
</Controller>
</RSLogix5000Content>
